#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The product validation manifest, run explicitly rather than by git hooks.
#
# Usage: scripts/validate [AREA] [--changed BASE | --full] [--list] [--skip-unprepared]
#        scripts/validate --prepare-catalog-inputs
#        scripts/validate package|nix --input-hash
#   --input-hash prints the SHA256 of the area's declared repository inputs
#   and this selector, including uncommitted files, without running checks.
#   Nightly uses it to identify a passing container build. It reads no base.
#   AREA is one of: logic, manifests, boundary, cli, tools, repo, offline,
#   unit, package, qml, nix, all (default: all). One area per call.
#   repo holds the checks this file makes itself, the whitespace
#   row, the self-check that every scripts/test-* file has a row, the
#   check that nothing under bin/ or shell/ loads a file under scripts/, the
#   check that no file under bin/, shell/ or config/ writes a monitor rule,
#   the check that no file in the tree holds a PEM private key and the md-refs
#   check of every markdown reference and source citation;
#   scripts/test-validate.sh, under tools, is their control. tools also
#   holds the document byte ceiling check this file makes, selected, unlike
#   a repo row, only when a Markdown file, a file under docs/ or the
#   doc-limits configuration changes; test-validate.sh is its control too.
#   unit runs the QML unit tests, which need Qt and no Wayland session;
#   package builds and installs the Arch recipes in a podman container; nix
#   builds the flake in a container, which needs podman or docker and the
#   network; offline excludes unit, package, nix, nested smoke and the
#   explicitly network-enabled publication row.
#   --changed BASE selects rows whose inputs changed against BASE, including
#   staged, unstaged and untracked files. Renames include both paths. A
#   wildcard input of a qml row or a nested smoke row matches a Markdown
#   file under shell/ only when it ends in .md: index_add. Unknown
#   inputs or an unreadable diff select the whole area. Repository checks
#   always run, except a Markdown/text-only diff selects only text checks,
#   including when the product displays that text. --list prints selected
#   commands without executing them.
#   Without a scope flag, compare against this area's last pass in this
#   worktree, the newest commit since the branch point that holds the tree
#   the last passing run read, else the default branch's merge base.
#   --full explicitly selects every row in the area.
#   A row's input `$NAME` is an environment input it cannot run without,
#   prepared state such as local models; it matches no path. Such a row run
#   with NAME unset exits 77. --skip-unprepared, for a host that holds no
#   prepared state, selects no row whose `$NAME` input is unset or empty and
#   prints `validate: unselected unset=<NAME> row=<label>` on stderr; such a
#   run records no last pass, `validate: last-pass=unrecorded
#   reason=unselected`.
#   A row's input `device:GLOB` requires a character device matching GLOB.
#   --skip-unprepared leaves it unselected when none exists and prints
#   `validate: unselected missing=device:GLOB row=<label>` on stderr.
#   A row's input `bus:user` requires a socket at $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bus, a
#   user bus. --skip-unprepared leaves it unselected when none exists and
#   prints `validate: unselected missing=bus:user row=<label>` on stderr.
#   A row's input `%scope` says it reads VGS_VALIDATE_BASE and
#   VGS_VALIDATE_CHANGED to narrow its own work; it matches no path, and
#   only such a row's record binds the base and the scope.
#   A row's input `@NAME` names state it shares with every other row that
#   names it, a fixed file, socket or container; it matches no path. Rows
#   that share a `@NAME` never run at the same time, and a row whose input
#   is `@alone` runs with no other row beside it.
#   A row's input `%weight=N` names how many cores the row keeps busy at
#   once, N a positive integer, and `%weight=all` says its own jobs fan
#   out over every core; a row without one weighs 1, and a row heavier than
#   the core count weighs the core count. It matches no path. Another
#   value refuses the run with exit 2, `validate: refused: weight=<value>
#   row=<label>`.
#   A run that compares prints `validate: base=<commit> source=<source>` on
#   stderr, the source one of argument, DEV_VALIDATE_BASE,
#   VGS_VALIDATE_BASE, last-pass or merge-base, in that precedence.
#   A run that passes (exit 0) on the merge base, the last pass or --full
#   records the tree it read, tracked and untracked files git does not
#   ignore, committed or not, as this area's last pass in
#   <git-dir>/vgs-validated-<area> when that tree is the same at its start
#   and end, and prints `validate: last-pass=recorded` or
#   `validate: last-pass=unrecorded reason=<reason>`: last_pass_record.
#   Every executed row prints `validate: secs=<seconds> exit=<status> row=<label>`.
#   The selected rows of one run go side by side while at most
#   VGS_VALIDATE_JOBS run and their weights in flight fit the core count,
#   nproc. With more than one job they start heaviest first, table order
#   breaking ties, and an `@alone` row keeps its place in the table; a row
#   whose weight would pass the core count waits, and so does every row
#   after it in that order. Each row's lines from `== <label>` to
#   its secs line print whole in table order; with more than one job, a
#   row not marked `@alone` prints its stderr there on stdout: the run
#   loop below.
#   A diff-scoped run selects the nested smoke when its own inputs match a
#   changed path or one reaches a smoke row, whatever table row owns it
#   (smoke_table_reach), and passes it the rows the
#   change reaches as `scripts/qml-smoke.sh --rows <row>,...`, or no --rows
#   for every row, and prints `validate: smoke-rows=some selected=<n>
#   total=<m>` or `validate: smoke-rows=all reason=<reason>`, the
#   `validate: smoke-input ...` self-check lines and one `validate:
#   load-unread path=<file> line=<n> site=<kind>` line for each load site
#   no directive covers that leaves a smoke row untraced, on stderr:
#   smoke_rows_selected below. An untraced smoke row selects the nested
#   smoke on every change but a text-only one. Those lines leave that run's
#   exit status alone; the tools row `validation inputs are read` fails on a
#   `smoke-input malformed` or `smoke-input unparsed` line and exits 77 when
#   the reading could not run. It also checks that manual table inputs
#   carry a reason: smoke_reads_named below.
#   A table row selects by its command files, their direct loads and
#   in-process closure, and its reasoned input globs. A site that reading
#   cannot trace runs its row without pass reuse on every non-text change,
#   with `validate: load-unread path=<file> line=<n> site=<kind>`. A failed
#   read makes every ordinary row required and untraced, with
#   `validate: selection=full reason=table-loads-<fact> ...`.
#   Each row that ends, and each nested smoke row, records its outcome and
#   seconds in <git-dir>/vgs-validated-rows as it ends, and a selected row
#   a recorded pass covers is reused and not run, by the rule in
#   docs/architecture/validation.md § Selection: the row records below. A
#   run prints each selected row as `validate: reused secs=<s>
#   row=<label>` or `validate: rerun secs=<s> [reason=<reason>]
#   row=<label>`, smoke=<row> for a smoke row, with its last recorded
#   seconds or `unknown`, then `validate: reuse=on rows-reused=<n> ...`
#   with the totals, or `validate: reuse=off reason=<reason>`, --full among
#   the reasons, and `validate: smoke-reuse=off reason=<reason>` when what
#   a smoke row's reach rests on cannot be read.
#
# VGS_VALIDATE_BASE: the commit the whitespace row diffs the tree against;
#   used as the default change base too, ahead of the last pass. --changed
#   and DEV_VALIDATE_BASE override it. Unset,
#   whitespace_base below resolves the base; an unavailable base exits 77.
# DEV_VALIDATE_BASE: the fix-round base supplied by Kendex; used when neither
#   --changed nor --full is present, ahead of VGS_VALIDATE_BASE and the last
#   pass.
# VGS_VALIDATE_CHANGED: on a readable diff-scoped run, the NUL-delimited file
#   of changed paths a row may read to narrow its own work. Unset means
#   everything changed.
# VGS_VALIDATE_JOBS: how many rows run at once at most, a positive integer;
#   unset or empty is the core count, nproc. The rows' weights bound them
#   further. 1 runs the rows one after another, each printing as it runs.
# VGS_VALIDATE_LOADS_SECS: the deadline of the table rows' load reading in
#   seconds, 120 when unset: table_loads_read below.
# The document byte ceiling row reads no base: --changed, VGS_VALIDATE_BASE,
#   DEV_VALIDATE_BASE and the last pass only choose whether it runs.
#
# Exit 0: every selected check passed. Exit 77: every check that ran passed
# but at least one could not run and is named; that is not a pass. Exit 1: a
# check failed. Exit 2: invalid area or arguments, named by
# `validate: refused: area=`, `extra-argument=` or
#   `changed-base=missing-or-repeated` or `scope=conflicting-or-repeated`,
#   or an invalid VGS_VALIDATE_JOBS, `validate: refused: jobs=<value>`,
#   or a row's invalid weight, `validate: refused: weight=<value> row=<label>`.
# A run that prints its verdict line, `validate: ok`, `validate: failed=` or
#   `validate: status=not-measured skipped=`, prints
#   `validate: lanes=<area> selection=<value>` after it, the line
#   `orch-runtime validate entry --record` reads: battery when the run left
#   out no row of its area, all when the changed paths, the text-only filter or the
#   rebased scope stood rows down or its rows were handed
#   VGS_VALIDATE_CHANGED, and subset when --skip-unprepared left out a row
#   as well. A reused row counts as run. A `validate: row-records=` line
#   from the exit trap can follow it, and --record then reads that run as
#   unreported.
# Every end of validate bash can see stops the running rows first: an INT,
#   TERM, HUP or QUIT, which exit 130, 143, 129 or 131, and a fatal signal
#   bash takes for its EXIT trap, such as a PIPE. Each row's process group
#   gets TERM, then KILL once 10 s have passed or at a repeat signal. Once
#   the nested smoke's group has ended, or the 10 s have passed, its per-row
#   results are recorded and the run's scratch root is removed, without
#   waiting on the other rows, so the removal fits the stop of a unit that
#   KILLs 10 s after its TERM. A KILL to validate itself cannot be caught:
#   it leaves the running rows going, its scratch root, and the smoke's
#   results for the next run to record. Each world still owns its row's
#   root.
# Each run keeps all its scratch under one root in TMPDIR, named for its
#   owner: validate-<pid>-<start>-<pid namespace>-r.XXXXXX. Before it makes
#   it, a run removes the root of each run whose owner has ended
#   (reap_orphans in scripts/smoke/reap.sh) and prints its
#   `validate: cleanup=` lines on stderr. A root of the older
#   validate-<pid>-XXXXXXXX form, a directory or a file, goes only when its
#   pid is absent, it is older than 10800 s and no process holds it. A
#   root that cannot be made exits 1 with
#   `validate: scratch-root=failed reason=<reason>`.
set -euo pipefail
# A read pipes its git command into mapfile, so pipefail gives the read that
# command's status, and lastpipe keeps mapfile's array in this shell.
# lastpipe holds only while job control is off (bash(1), shopt), and
# start_row turns it on only to start a row. A process substitution keeps
# no such status: a wait on it fails once Bash has reaped it.
shopt -s lastpipe

self="$(readlink -f -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")"
repo="$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "$self")/.." && pwd)"
cd -- "$repo"
# Every row runs under the test-run marker, so the theme judge refuses a
# reload hook that could reach the host's live applications:
# docs/architecture/validation.md.
export VGS_TEST_RUN=1

# Private row re-entry carries selection as data. The parent alone selects
# rows and records a last pass; the child only loads this file's checks.
row_entry=false
if [[ ${1-} == --row ]]; then
  row_entry=true
  export VGS_VALIDATE_BASE="$2"
  row_path_count="$3"
  shift 3
  row_paths=()
  if ((row_path_count >= 0)); then
    row_paths=("${@:1:row_path_count}")
    shift "$row_path_count"
  fi
  shift # the command separator
  row_words=("$@")
  set --
fi

area="all"
area_given=false
change_base=""
list_only=false
full_scope=false
input_hash=false
skip_unprepared=false
unselected=false
catalog_prepare_only=false
catalog_listings=""
runtime_cache=""
if [[ $# == 1 && $1 == --prepare-catalog-inputs ]]; then
  catalog_prepare_only=true
  set --
fi
while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]; do
  case "$1" in
    --changed)
      if [[ $full_scope == true ]]; then
        echo 'validate: refused: scope=conflicting-or-repeated' >&2; exit 2
      fi
      if [[ $# -lt 2 || -z $2 || $2 == -* || -n $change_base ]]; then
        echo 'validate: refused: changed-base=missing-or-repeated' >&2; exit 2
      fi
      change_base="$2"; shift 2 ;;
    --full)
      if [[ $full_scope == true || -n $change_base ]]; then
        echo 'validate: refused: scope=conflicting-or-repeated' >&2; exit 2
      fi
      full_scope=true; shift ;;
    --list) list_only=true; shift ;;
    --input-hash) input_hash=true; shift ;;
    --skip-unprepared) skip_unprepared=true; shift ;;
    *)
      if [[ $area_given == true ]]; then
        printf 'validate: refused: extra-argument=%s\none area per call\n' "$1" >&2; exit 2
      fi
      area="$1"; area_given=true; shift ;;
  esac
done
case "$area" in
  logic|manifests|boundary|cli|tools|repo|offline|unit|package|qml|nix|all) ;;
  *) printf 'validate: refused: area=%s\n' "$area" >&2; exit 2 ;;
esac
if [[ $input_hash == true ]]; then
  if [[ $area != package && $area != nix ]] || [[ $full_scope == true || -n $change_base || $list_only == true || $skip_unprepared == true ]]; then
    echo 'validate: refused: input-hash=requires-package-or-nix-only' >&2; exit 2
  fi
  full_scope=true
fi
# The core count bounds the weight of the rows in flight. nproc reads the
# CPU affinity and a cgroup v2 CPU quota, and OMP_NUM_THREADS sets its
# answer (coreutils, `info coreutils 'nproc invocation'`), which the
# scheduler's control uses for a stand-in count.
cores="$(nproc)"
jobs_max="${VGS_VALIDATE_JOBS:-}"
if [[ -z $jobs_max ]]; then
  jobs_max="$cores"
elif [[ ! $jobs_max =~ ^[1-9][0-9]*$ ]]; then
  printf 'validate: refused: jobs=%s\n' "$jobs_max" >&2; exit 2
fi
failed=()
skipped=()
# A scratch file, or with -d a directory, under scratch_root: the run's root,
# or in a row entry the world's temporary directory, which the world
# removes with the row. mktemp makes it by exclusive creation: the holders
# of one run share the root and run side by side, so a name picked first
# and created after can go to two of them, and the one that removes it
# first leaves the other with no file.
scratch_root=""
scratch_make() { # [-d]
  mktemp "$@" -- "$scratch_root/scratch.XXXXXXXX"
}
scratch_file() { scratch_make; }
scratch_dir() { scratch_make -d; }

# node on PATH may be a version-manager shim that reads the caller's own
# configuration and refuses under a row's temporary home, so each row reaches
# node through a link to the binary it resolves to here.
node_bin=""
if command -v node >/dev/null; then
  node_bin="$(node -e 'process.stdout.write(process.execPath)')" ||
    { echo 'validate: node=unresolved' >&2; exit 1; }
fi

# The world owns each row's home, XDG directories, scratch and cleanup.
# docs/architecture/validation.md § Test isolation.
# Package and nix use their own containers and keep the caller's image
# store. The world's control runs outside so it can test the actual boundary.
run() { # SCRATCH WORLD-OWNER LABEL CMD...
  local row_home="$1" owner="${2:-row}" label="$3" started status elapsed
  local path_count=-1 paths=() declarations=(--fresh) cache_input=""
  shift 3
  if [[ $1 == catalog_wallpaper_names ]]; then
    declarations+=(--input "$catalog_listings")
    set -- "$@" "$catalog_listings"
  fi
  if [[ $1 == scripts/test-jarvis-selftest.sh ]]; then
    declarations+=(--input "$runtime_cache")
    cache_input="$runtime_cache"
  fi
  echo "== $label"
  started=$SECONDS
  status=0
  (
    if [[ $owner == container || $owner == control ]]; then
      mkdir -- "$row_home" || exit 1
      trap 'chmod -R u+rwX -- "$row_home" 2>/dev/null; rm -rf -- "${row_home:?}"' EXIT
      export XDG_CONFIG_HOME="$row_home/.config" GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL="$row_home/gitconfig"
      [[ -z $node_bin ]] || export PATH="${node_bin%/*}:$PATH"
      "$@"
    elif [[ $owner == entry ]]; then
      # A parallel packaging row cannot stop a nested entry from starting.
      "$repo/scripts/smoke/gpu-fence.sh" --fresh -- node "$repo/scripts/check-packaging.js" --installed-engine || exit "$?"
      # Graphical runners own their output declarations before world entry.
      "$@"
    else
      [[ $owner != network ]] || declarations+=(--net)
      [[ -z $cache_input ]] || export AGENT_RUNTIME_CACHE="$cache_input"
      if [[ -n ${VGS_VALIDATE_CHANGED:-} ]]; then
        mapfile -d '' -t paths <"$VGS_VALIDATE_CHANGED" || exit 1
        path_count=${#paths[@]}
      fi
      "$repo/scripts/smoke/gpu-fence.sh" "${declarations[@]}" -- "$BASH" "$self" --row "${VGS_VALIDATE_BASE:-}" "$path_count" "${paths[@]}" -- "$@"
    fi
  ) || status=$?
  elapsed=$((SECONDS - started))
  printf 'validate: secs=%s exit=%s row=%s\n' "$elapsed" "$status" "$label"
  return "$status"
}

catalog_input_prepare() {
  local status=0
  catalog_listings="$(realpath -m -- "${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/vgshell/validate/theme-listings")" || return 1
  printf 'validate: input-step=catalog path=%q\n' "$catalog_listings"
  node "$repo/scripts/check-catalog-wallpaper-names.js" --prepare "$repo/themes" "$catalog_listings" || status=$?
  if [[ $status == 0 && ! -d $catalog_listings ]]; then
    echo 'validate: input-step=failed name=catalog reason=missing-output' >&2
    return 1
  fi
  if [[ $status != 0 ]]; then
    printf 'validate: input-step=failed name=catalog exit=%s\n' "$status" >&2
  fi
  return "$status"
}

# The kendex runtimes the Jarvis self-test controls run, built or found
# built in the caller's cache by orch's setup before the row enters the
# world, whose HOME and cache are its own and which has no build toolchain.
# The row reads that cache through a read-only input AGENT_RUNTIME_CACHE
# names.
runtime_input_prepare() {
  local built status=0
  built="$("$repo/.agents/skills/orch/scripts/setup" 2>&1)" || status=$?
  if [[ $status != 0 ]]; then
    printf '%s\n' "$built" >&2
    printf 'validate: input-step=failed name=kendex-runtimes exit=%s\n' "$status" >&2
    return 1
  fi
  runtime_cache="$("$BASH" -c '. "$1" && agent_runtime_cache' _ "$repo/.agents/skills/agent-runtime/scripts/lib/key.sh")" &&
    runtime_cache="$(realpath -e -- "$runtime_cache")" ||
    { echo 'validate: input-step=failed name=kendex-runtimes reason=missing-output' >&2; return 1; }
  printf 'validate: input-step=kendex-runtimes path=%q\n' "$runtime_cache"
}

catalog_wallpaper_names() {
  node "$repo/scripts/check-catalog-wallpaper-names.js" "$repo/themes" "$1"
}

# Rows: area | label | command | additional input globs, space-delimited,
# and the `$NAME` environment inputs, `@NAME` shared state and `%scope` and
# `%weight=` declarations the header names | world owner (default row) |
# reason for the manual inputs, if any.
# A weight counts the most the row runs at once: the processes of a nested
# world (driver, sink, Hyprland, Quickshell: 4), a runner beside its
# qmltestrunner (2), a build's fixed -j8 (8), a fixed number of children
# or jobs that work side by side, or `all` for jobs bounded by the core
# count or by a list that grows with the tree. A stand-in server or a
# child that waits on the test does not count. An entry owns its world's
# declarations; network retains the world with live network access; a
# container supplies its own boundary. The world's control needs the
# caller's writable checkout to prove entry and read-only checks.
# Command files, their direct loads and their in-process imports are inputs
# without a declaration. Keep manual patterns for what a run or copy reads
# beyond that boundary, with the reason beside the declaration. A runner's
# own control uses %harness= to select only by the harness it tests.
rows=(
  # An `@alone` row starts once every row above it has ended, so it goes
  # first: below the rest it would hold every row after it behind a drain.
  "nix|nix flake package|scripts/test-flake.sh|flake.nix flake.lock packaging/arch/vgshell-quickshell/* packaging/install-system.sh packaging/install-tree.manifest scripts/check-install-tree.sh bin/* shell/* config/* themes/* @alone|container|the container builds the flake and its source tree"
  "logic|duration formatter|node scripts/test-duration.js|"
  "logic|timestamp formatter|node scripts/test-timestamp.js|"
  "logic|page reference reader|node scripts/test-page-reference.js|"
  "logic|traffic counters rates and bounded apps|node scripts/test-traffic-logic.js|"
  "logic|network snapshot decisions|node scripts/test-network-logic.js|"
  "logic|network QR secret transport controls|python3 scripts/test-network-share.py|"
  "logic|network join secret transport and cleanup controls|scripts/test-network-enterprise.sh|scripts/smoke/fixtures/devices/network-join-nmcli.py||the test runs the network join helper with a copied nmcli stand-in"
  "logic|Tailscale decisions|node scripts/test-tailscale-logic.js|"
  "logic|VPN decisions|node scripts/test-vpn-logic.js|"
  "logic|tray decisions|node scripts/test-tray-logic.js|"
  "logic|printers decisions|node scripts/test-printers-logic.js|"
  "logic|plugin logic table|node scripts/test-plugin-logic.js|shell/assets/sounds/*||computed path - validateManifest resolves sound files from the manifest and its installation folder"
  "logic|pads and list settings judge|node scripts/test-pads.js|"
  "logic|plugin status judge|node scripts/test-plugin-status.js|shell/plugins/vgs.notifications/manifest.json shell/plugins/vgs.sound/manifest.json||computed path - statusWorld joins its plugin folder parameter with manifest.json"
  "logic|plugin menu judge|node scripts/test-plugin-menu.js|"
  "logic|key capture judge|node scripts/test-key-capture.js|"
  "logic|floating TUI logic table|node scripts/test-tui-logic.js|bin/vgshell-tui bin/lib/tui.sh||the shell TUI helper starts through bin/vgshell-tui and sources its library"
  "logic|ipc capability logic table|node scripts/test-ipc-logic.js|"
  "logic|requirement notice logic table|node scripts/test-notice-logic.js|"
  "logic|Hyprland layer logic|node scripts/test-hyprland-layer.js|themes/catalog/*||the suite runs the theme judge against catalog fixtures"
  "logic|Hyprland capability readings|node scripts/test-hyprland-state.js|shell/Commons/TuiArguments.js shell/Ui/icons/Lucide.js shell/Ui/icons/Own.js shell/Commons/SettingValues.js shell/Commons/PageReference.js||the mutation control runs HyprlandState.js in a copied shell tree"
  "cli|layer glass managed TUI|scripts/test-layer-glass-tui.sh|shell/Core/HyprlandState.js shell/Core/HyprlandLayer.js shell/Core/MonitorLogic.js shell/Core/Dispatch.js shell/Core/ConfigLogic.js shell/Core/PackageManagers.js||the TUI runs the Hyprland judge through the VGS CLI fixture"
  "logic|core input facts|node scripts/test-input-facts.js|shell/Core/PluginLogic.js shell/Commons/TuiArguments.js shell/Core/Pads.js shell/Core/PackageReview.js shell/Commons/SettingValues.js shell/Commons/PageReference.js shell/Ui/icons/Lucide.js shell/Ui/icons/Own.js||the mutation control copies shell/Core, shell/Commons and the icons"
  "logic|active XKB input identities|python3 -I scripts/test-xkb-keys.py|"
  "logic|monitor outputs reading|node scripts/test-monitor-logic.js|"
  "cli|display guard|scripts/test-display-guard.sh|"
  "logic|dispatch table|node scripts/test-dispatch.js|"
  "logic|instance lifetime cleanup|node scripts/test-lifetime.js|"
  "logic|library loader controls|node scripts/test-qml-library.js|shell/Commons/TuiArguments.js||the child Node process evaluates the copied QML library import closure"
  "logic|rounded inset helper|node scripts/test-inset.js|"
  "logic|setting value helper|node scripts/test-setting-values.js|"
  "logic|session lock reading|node scripts/test-session-lock-state.js|"
  "logic|desktop launch rule|node scripts/test-desktop-launch.js|"
  "logic|icon painted extent|node scripts/test-icon-bounds.js|"
  "logic|theme judge table|node scripts/test-theme-logic.js|shell/Ui/controls/FormRow.qml shell/plugins/vgs.notifications/NotificationCard.qml shell/plugins/vgs.notifications/MediaSlot.qml shell/plugins/vgs.notifications/RowMeasure.qml||computed path - fs.readFileSync joins the checkout with each LED_LINES file"
